What is Nmap?
Nmap stands for Network Mapper. It is a powerful and widely used open-source tool for network discovery and security auditing.
Key Purposes of Nmap:
Discover devices (hosts) on a network
Identify open ports on those devices
Detect services running on ports (e.g., HTTP, FTP)
Determine the operating system (OS) and version of devices
Perform vulnerability scanning using scripts
Map network topology
